# Test: a daemon start over stored DNS answers resolves only the names whose
#       stored answer expired, and programs the others from the store.
# Spec: spec-fetched-data-survives-restart -- Wiring Test row 7, AC-13, user
#       story 5
# QUESTION: does the daemon's own start (the handshake, OnStarted, the store
#           read, schedule.reset, the refresh worker) honour the expires-at the
#           previous run wrote? A unit test drives configure and the worker
#           over a store it seeded itself (TestStartDoesNotResolveAnUnexpiredName);
#           only a second real start proves the expiry survives the process
#           and that the handshake does not arm every name due at once.
# VALIDATES: the group whose stored answer is an hour from expiry (alpha) is
#            not asked for at start and keeps the address the first run
#            stored; the group whose stored answer expired (zulu) is asked for
#            at start.
# PREVENTS: a reboot that asks upstream for every name, and so can enforce
#           different addresses than the box enforced before it.
#
# The fixture is domainGroupRestartKeepsAnswers
# (internal/test/fixture/netfilter_fixture_domain_group_restart.go). It serves
# the DNS stub in process on 127.0.0.1:53, starts the daemon itself twice over
# one config directory (so one store), and logs every question the stub
# receives. Between the starts it waits for the daemon's table to leave the
# kernel, so the set read after the second start cannot be the first run's
# left behind, and it changes both answers, so an address from the second
# answer in alpha's set says alpha was asked again. It returns an error for
# every check that fails (fixture.Run reports it), and prints the markers
# below only after all of them held.
#
# alpha sorts before zulu (lessKey, schedule.go), so a start that made every
# unit due would ask for alpha BEFORE the zulu answer the fixture waits for:
# the absence of an alpha query is then observable, not a race.
#
# The fixture binds port 53 and the daemon it starts programs nftables, so the
# file needs CAP_NET_ADMIN and CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE.
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-bind
# Port 53 and the nftables ruleset are node-wide; see
# test/plugin/firewall-domain-group-update.ci for why one group covers both.
option=exclusive:group=dns-stub-port-53
option=timeout:value=90s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/firewall-domain-group-restart-keeps-answers:timeout=85s
expect=exit:code=0

# alpha's set after the second start holds the address the first run stored.
expect=stdout:contains=domain_v4_alpha
expect=stdout:contains=203.0.113.20
# The fixture checked the stub's query log: zulu was asked, alpha was not.
expect=stdout:contains=restart-asked-for zulu.example.test not alpha.example.test
